<title>FINLAND: Enso, Metsaliitto plan to up pulp price.</title>
<headline>Enso, Metsaliitto plan to up pulp price.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish pulp producers Enso Oy and Metsaliitto group said on Tuesday they are planning to follow Swedish Sodra by raising prices of softwood market pulp to $610 per tonne from $560 at the beginning of 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;We are most likely to do so as paper production is at a high level,&quot; Simo Pesola, managing director of Enso's pulp marketing subsidiary Enso Fibres told Reuters by telephone, when asked whether Enso would follow Sweden's Sodra, which announced long fibre pulp price hikes on Monday.</p>
</text>
